        "Paul’s rhetoric becomes especially sharp in 5:12 when he wishes the agitators would “mutilate” or “emasculate” themselves. This is polemical hyperbole in a heated controversy, not a model for Christian mockery, bodily threats, or crude attacks on opponents. The paragraph then turns decisively toward love: freedom is not an opportunity for the flesh but a calling to serve one another."
